  message: "Fixed in PR #362 (dev 86bb6f0444), Wave-3 Phase-2 §C entrypoint F5 (exportedness gate). Root cause: entrypoints.py library_export branch emitted LIBRARY_EXPORT on any symbol carrying the library_export concept with no exportedness check. Fix: gate the branch on INV-jusot's canonical Symbol.visibility axis (computed in finalize step 7b, before detect_entrypoints at cli.py:8877, so it is populated at detection time) — skip when visibility is affirmatively non-public, permissive on None. Keys on the visibility axis per plan §E-5 (now unblocked by INV-jusot); the filed 'cannot use is_exported — None for 100% of nodes' caveat is stale post-INV-jusot. serialization_callback (Go reflective callbacks, WI-pimig) deliberately left ungated.\n\nBehavioral evidence — re-ran the item's OWN filed repro (fresh hypergumbo run on a /tmp fixture: public fold_string_interpolation with a nested private _sub closure passed to re.sub) on merged dev with the editable binary (which hypergumbo = /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo/.venv/bin/hypergumbo):\n  BEFORE: library_export EPs = ['fold_string_interpolation' (public, conf 1.0), 'fold_string_interpolation._sub' (private, conf 0.9465)]\n  AFTER:  library_export EPs = ['fold_string_interpolation' (public, conf 1.0)] — _sub suppressed (visibility=private, is_exported=False), public export retained.\nProduction-path test (test_entrypoints.py): test_library_export_skipped_for_non_public_visibility (visibility=private -> no LIBRARY_EXPORT) + test_library_export_kept_for_public_visibility (positive control). Full affected suite 15620 passed, entrypoints.py 100% coverage."  # 0c72
